---
/**
 * The hover preview island: a script, and nothing else.
 *
 * It renders no markup on purpose. The excerpt is already in the page, on the
 * anchors, and the card is built in the browser and appended to `<body>` —
 * which is also why its styles live in `src/styles/base.css` rather than in a
 * scoped `<style>` here: Astro's scoping cannot reach an element the script
 * invents.
 *
 * The component exists in order to be *conditionally imported*. A bare
 * `<script>` in `Note.astro` behind `{config.features.hoverPreview && …}` would
 * still ship: Astro hoists and bundles component scripts at compile time
 * regardless of the surrounding conditional. Only dropping the import takes the
 * script out of the module graph. See `JOTTER_HOVER_PREVIEW` in
 * `astro.config.ts`, and the same trap documented beside `JOTTER_GRAPH`.
 */
---

<script>
  import '../scripts/hover-preview.js'
</script>
